        <mxCell id="m24" value="PUT /roles/{role_code}/permissions" style="html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;rounded=0;curved=0;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="495" y="1750" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="700" y="1750" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m25" value="assert user:manage ∈ permissions — identity resolves its own&lt;br&gt;permission from the same cache, never special-cased (db-identity)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=middle;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="751" y="1811" /><mxPoint x="751" y="1835" /></Array><mxPoint x="710" y="1811" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="710" y="1835" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m26" value="tx: DELETE + INSERT role_permission (role_id, permission_id)&lt;br&gt;+ INSERT outbox('audit.recorded') — every grant and revoke is traced" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=middle;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="751" y="1886" /><mxPoint x="751" y="1910" /></Array><mxPoint x="710" y="1886" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="710" y="1910" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m27" value="SET perm:role:{code} = [recomputed permissions] · TTL 6h" style="html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;rounded=0;curved=0;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="710" y="1994" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="915" y="1994" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m28" value="SET fails or Redis is down ⇒ log + metric, swallow the error&lt;br&gt;the response is still 200 · the hourly sweep repairs the key" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=middle;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="751" y="2055" /><mxPoint x="751" y="2079" /></Array><mxPoint x="710" y="2055" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="710" y="2079" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m29" value="200 {role_code, permissions[]}" style="html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;rounded=0;curved=0;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;endSize=8;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="700" y="2167" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="495" y="2167" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="m30" value="200" style="html=1;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;rounded=0;curved=0;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;endSize=8;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="485" y="2213" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="280" y="2213" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt0" value="§M1: the sweep runs whether or not anything changed. Rewrite-on-change-only would let an idle role's key expire with no trigger left to rewrite it." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="291" width="320" height="74" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt1" value="The status assert is the whole deactivation mechanism: users are never deleted, only flipped to DISABLED (db-identity.md). Without it a disabled account still receives a valid token — the ListUsersByRole ACTIVE filter only stops them being *assigned*, not authenticated. Residual, accepted: a token already issued stays valid until exp; disable does not blacklist the live jti." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="539" width="320" height="144" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt2" value="JWT claims (registry §6): sub, username, full_name, department, roles[], jti, exp. roles[] only — never permissions[], which would go stale until re-login (D11)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="693" width="320" height="74" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt3" value="Redis down here fails closed as well: the blacklist cannot be consulted, so the token cannot be shown to be un-revoked. Same policy, same reason, as the permission cache below — Redis is already a hard auth dependency (§M1)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="991" width="320" height="102" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt4" value="Services trust those headers because the 80xx REST port is reachable only through the gateway (D16) — the gRPC 505x port is not routed at all. Header names are a registry delta." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="1103" width="320" height="88" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt5" value="Redis unavailable ⇒ PERMISSION_DENIED, fail closed (§M1). Deliberately unlike D9's self-heal: a missed expiry warning costs nothing, a wrongly-granted permission is an incident." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="1282" width="320" height="88" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt6" value="The fragment is 'opt' and the failure is swallowed on purpose: Redis is NOT on this request's success path. It cannot join the Postgres transaction, and letting a cache write fail an authorization change that is already committed would report a lie to the admin and invite a retry that re-writes role_permission for no reason. Contrast seq-01's read path, where Redis being down is fail-closed PERMISSION_DENIED — enforcement must fail shut, propagation must not fail the write." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="2251" width="320" height="172" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt7" value="This is the path that actually delivers revocation; the hourly loop at the top is what BOUNDS it. If this SET is missed, the sweep repairs the key within 1h (TTL 6h is the last-resort backstop, not the mechanism). Net guarantee: bounded eventual revocation (§M1), never immediacy — nothing in the requirement asks for immediacy, only for better than 'wait for re-login'." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="2433" width="320" height="144" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="nt8" value="One role key, every holder at once — the map is keyed by role, not by user, which is why a revoke needs no per-user fan-out. The asymmetric case: assigning or removing a user's ROLE writes only user_role and touches Redis not at all, because roles[] is a JWT claim — that change lands at the user's next login, not on this request (db-identity, §M1)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#e0b400;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1245" y="2587" width="320" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
